<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28379" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Medullĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Medullum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little town in Latium</i>, near the
			modern <i>Monte Verde</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 33,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, § 68</span></i>.
			—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Medullīnus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Medullia, Medullian;</i> as <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdullīnus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i>a Roman surname;</i> e. g. L. Furius
			Medullinus, <i><span class="en">Liv. 4, 25, 5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdullīna</span></b> ,
				ae, f.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Livia Medullina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 322</span></i>.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Medullīni</span></b> , ōrum,
				m., <i>inhabitants of Medullia</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 535</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
